  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Homeland Security spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security has obligated $69.1B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security recorded 30,042 awards with an average award size of $2.3M. The Department of Homeland Security’s obligations are up 143.7% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Homeland Security buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security buys construction, shipbuilding, security services, logistics consulting, and IT and engineering services. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $30.3B, Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $7.9B, Security Guards and Patrol Services accounts for $4.3B, Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services accounts for $3.2B, and Other Computer Related Services and Computer Systems Design Services each account for $2.5B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Homeland Security's largest contractors?",
      "a": "FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO is the largest DHS contractor at $13.4B. Other top contractors include BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED at $4.5B, DAVIE DEFENSE INC. at $3.5B, SOUTHWEST VALLEY CONSTRUCTORS CO at $2.5B, and SLS FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $2.4B."
